{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/765494-monotheistic-is-it-possible","id":765494,"title":"Monotheistic: is it possible?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-14T05:24:23-08:00","id":765494,"title":"Monotheistic: is it possible?","content":"Does anybody have any thoughts on the possibility that a Scion who rises to godhood abandons their ties to a pantheon completely and establishes themselves as the soul deity of their cult? I understand this might be a bit complicated as it would effectively mean they're defending their overworld and underworld singlehandedly against the Titans, but could it be done, regardless? Scions of such a god might be viewed as saints or prophets by their parent's followers, but the belief in true divinity would fall to their parent alone.<br /> <br /> I know that Scion focuses more on the polytheistic religions. But in a world where gods openly clash with one another, I find it unlikely that there hasn't been at least one cult stepping forward who denounces the others as false gods or attributes them to being avatars of their lord.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-14T05:32:17-08:00","id":765497,"title":"","content":"I'd say this pretty much gives the Scion away to whichever Titan finds him or her first. Even now, some gods are corrupted by the influence of the Titans and that is with them having people to talk to, at least theoretically. A Scion who does such a radical step would very quickly end up as prey for the Titans to kill or worst. If memory serves, thats what happened to some of the lesser known Pantheons. They got torn apart, quite literally, because they didn't have sufficent Legend to defend themselves in the long run. So your Scions new religion would have to grow rapidly very quickly to fuel such a daring endeavour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8325-asmael","name":"Asmael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-14T07:05:38-08:00","id":765539,"title":"","content":"It wouldn't have to be a monotheistic point of view; it could also be henotheism (worship of one god, though the existence of others is granted).<br /> <br /> Neall likes the idea that exclusionary monotheism - the idea that there is only one god, denying the existence of others - originated with Aten, Titan of Light. Going with that, any god promulgating the idea is at the very least going to get the side-eye from other gods, if not investigated for Titanic corruption themselves.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-14T07:45:27-08:00","id":765553,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I figured somebody claiming they were the only divine would be facing an uphill battle, if not outright ganked upon leaving the house for work. I wanted to know if it was at all possible though, given that it seemed likely somebody had to have tried it at some point if history taught us anything about holy wars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T20:11:06-07:00","id":927424,"title":"","content":"I tend to view the missionary faiths: Buddhism, Christianity, Islam and Communism, as tools that any of the pantheons can co-opt for their personal use. This I use as my explanation for all the schisms. Yes, I did list Communism as a missionary faith. It doesn't really work as an economic theory, but it works very well as a cult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","name":"moonwolf8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T21:50:37-07:00","id":927445,"title":"","content":"For whatever it's worth, the evidence is that the Israelites before the Babylonian Captivity were more Henotheistic than Monotheistic. That works well and good for Judaism in the World into modern day thanks to being a specific cultural group. It's more complicated for Christianity because of being a proselytizing religion. It's plausible in the World, if unlike the spread of Christianity in our world, the faith operated more like an open Mystery Cults of the Roman Empire, and (for example) accepting salvation by Christ didn't require an active rejection of the existence of other gods, just the acceptance of Christ as one's salvation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 07-07-2016, 01:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T07:07:30-07:00","id":927601,"title":"","content":"Chiming in to agree about Henotheism. You could be worshiped over those other gods, but saying the other gods don't exist is strange and obviously untrue. I mean the Bible openly admits other gods exist while Islam transferred their divinity to the Jinn to explain their existence. Monotheism isn't the usual in history and while religious wars always existed, they were more My god can beat up your god rather than your god does not exist. Christianity, I think, is the first religion as an organization that ever tried to prove other gods false rather than inept.<br /> <br /> Of course, many seemingly polytheistic religions have monotheistic ties. You could do some sort of pantheism route, all gods are just different reflections of the same entity, or get so fate bound into a monotheistic religion, YOU become a prophet/saint/jinn rather than a god. Not to say the way you mentioned is impossible, but historically, Aten is perhaps the most likely outcome of such a venture if you don't take thousands of years to create a monotheistic religion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T10:24:35-07:00","id":927671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>moonwolf8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/765494-monotheistic-is-it-possible?p=927424#post927424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to view the missionary faiths: Buddhism, Christianity, Islam and Communism, as tools that any of the pantheons can co-opt for their personal use. This I use as my explanation for all the schisms. Yes, I did list Communism as a missionary faith. It doesn't really work as an economic theory, but it works very well as a cult.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I think the Titan of Light fills the role of Christianity, since it only has 1 avatar, is so bright mortals can't even look at them, and literally has friggen Angels serving at their command.<br /> <br /> <br /> ----------------------------------<br /> <br /> Actually, one of the first religions that tried to prove other gods were false was Judaism. They were originally polytheistic, but over the years, they invented the idea that all other gods in their pantheon were different avatars of the same god, which eventually became a monotheistic religion. Once you know this, it kind of explains all the contradictory actions their god has done by rationalizing it as being a different avatar going by the same name.<br /> <br /> <br /> ------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Also, I found out after posting this topic that there is a potential enemy group in the books (forgot which one) which attempts to use Fate Binding to merge all the gods into a single entity, and claims that Scions are just prophets, rather than children of the gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T11:34:58-07:00","id":927709,"title":"","content":"The Titan of Light as the Judeo-Christian god could work, or if you want to be henotheistic about it, you could say that YHWH is the sole surviving member of the Ugaritic pantheon, for one reason or the other, and that Jews are his worshippers, with Christians being a subset of his worshippers who worship Jesus of Nazareth as his son who became a god of redemption or mercy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T12:26:59-07:00","id":927737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/765494-monotheistic-is-it-possible?p=927671#post927671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, one of the first religions that tried to prove other gods were false was Judaism. They were originally polytheistic, but over the years, they invented the idea that all other gods in their pantheon were different avatars of the same god, which eventually became a monotheistic religion. Once you know this, it kind of explains all the contradictory actions their god has done by rationalizing it as being a different avatar going by the same name.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant more systematically. I know Judaism doesn't believe other gods exist, but I never heard of them going out of their way or as a group trying to prove they weren't real. Since Judaism isn't an evangelical religion, they usually don't seem to care if others have it &quot;wrong&quot; and try to discourage conversion at least a little. The only ones they usually try to convince are their own people. <br /> <br /> I don't like Aten representing the Judeo-Christian god as this puts many religions into a strange place. No way I can believe that most of the Loa serve or revere Aten. I've normally played it as the Judeo-Christian god got fatebound into being more distant than most since early in the bible he's having conversations and acting directly and later he's sending angels every time he wants to say a message. A religion with no one else in the pantheon to balance the fatebindings, he's stuck, especially with multiple cultures all over the globe putting their expectations on him. He exists and still sends others but rarely gets involved in anything. That means most of his agents are mortals sent weird epiphany's by angels, but there are enough mortals out there to cause any scion a headache.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T17:27:58-07:00","id":927857,"title":"","content":"<i>Lord of Light </i>is a good example of how one could do this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T21:16:48-07:00","id":927957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>3Comrades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/765494-monotheistic-is-it-possible?p=927601#post927601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Christianity, I think, is the first religion as an organization that ever tried to prove other gods false rather than inept.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe the Zoroastrians / The Yazata have Christianity beat by about six centuries in the very least in that regard.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Achaemenid Royal Inscription XPh - Xerxes</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I became king, there was among these countries one that was in rebellion. Ahura Mazda helped me. By the grace of Ahura Mazda I smote that country and put it in its place.<br /> <br /> And among these countries there was a place where previously the daiva [demons] were worshipped. Afterwards, by the grace of Ahura Mazda I destroyed that sanctuary of the daiva, and I proclaimed: 'The daiva shall not be worshipped!' Where previously the daiva were worshipped, there I worshipped Ahura Mazda at the proper time and in the proper manner.<br /> <br /> And there was something else that had been done wrong, and that too, I set right.<br /> <br /> That which I did, all I did by the grace of Ahura Mazda. Ahura Mazda helped me until I completed the work.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, in the very least the Persian Empire was quashing some religious groups, labeling their Divine Entities as Daiva, and destroying the temples in the name of their own Deity. While it isn't claiming they don't exist, it is claiming that a) they are not gods, b) they are fundamentally evil beings, and c) destroying the places of worship.<br /> <br /> Edit: I also expect they're not the first group to have done so, they're just the first group I know of. I would bet you that it has happened a lot, especially during early periods where different groups using entirely different cosmologies (such as an invading migrating group clashing with a native group) would claim that the other is actually just full of nonsense, especially if they were victorious and occult methods of defeating them proved non-functional. Either their magic or Divine Entity is stronger, or the lot they've just defeated were entirely confused and didn't have any actual magic or Divine Entity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 07-08-2016, 12:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T11:26:25-07:00","id":928297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neall likes the idea that exclusionary monotheism - the idea that there is only one god, denying the existence of others - originated with Aten, Titan of Light. Going with that, any god promulgating the idea is at the very least going to get the side-eye from other gods, if not investigated for Titanic corruption themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>I sure do, but I also like the idea that it functions as a cultural jammer for other pantheons to fuck with one another.<br /> <br /> Monotheism is in the World. It's still recognizably ours.<br /> <br /> 2e is changing the Second Titanomachy from straight-up Titans Bad, Gods Good into a Cold War type scenario, which gives you a lot more room for henotheistic, monolatric or monotheistic beliefs, even if the last is &quot;merely&quot; a subtle knife wielded by the gods of the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T15:52:36-07:00","id":928480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/765494-monotheistic-is-it-possible?p=928297#post928297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I sure do, but I also like the idea that it functions as a cultural jammer for other pantheons to fuck with one another.<br /> <br /> Monotheism is in the World. It's still recognizably ours.<br /> <br /> 2e is changing the Second Titanomachy from straight-up Titans Bad, Gods Good into a Cold War type scenario, which gives you a lot more room for henotheistic, monolatric or monotheistic beliefs, even if the last is &quot;merely&quot; a subtle knife wielded by the gods of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Ah, so it is theoretically possible to play on the side of Titans and still be a good guy? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I've also been told that in 2nd edition, the gods won't be overtly shaped by the belief of mortals. Which leads me to believe that just because mortals believe other gods don't exist, doesn't mean its true. I prefer this change, actually, as it means the players don't have to be so concerned with how their cult perceives them, and are free to be themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}